# File: tests/blender/test_rig_builtin_clips.py, tests/unit/test_builtin_clips.py
# Generated from: specs/136-add-a-built-in-procedural-clip-library-to-import-animations/requirements.md
Feature: Built-in procedural clip library for import_animations

  @SCN001
  Scenario: The built-in library bakes with no files
    Given a character rigged with rig_humanoid and no animation library folder
    When import_animations is called with library "builtin" and no clips
    Then the result is ok and every built-in clip is an action named after the clip on SK_<Name>
    And each action has keyframes on the bones its poses target, no file is read, and the rig is at rest

  @SCN002
  Scenario: The starter set is present
    Given the built-in library
    When all of its clips are baked
    Then the result lists Idle, FightIdle, Walk, Run, Punch1, Punch2, Punch3, Kick, Jump, JumpKick, Hit, Knockdown, Down, GetUp, Grab, Throw, Roar, Talk, and Ride

  @SCN003
  Scenario: A subset can be requested
    Given a rigged character
    When import_animations is called with library "builtin" and clips Idle and Walk
    Then only Idle and Walk are baked and listed

  @SCN004
  Scenario: One definition fits any proportions and A-pose angle
    Given a near-T-pose rig and a rig with arms 45 degrees below horizontal and different proportions
    When the same built-in clip is baked onto both
    Then at each key frame every targeted limb bone points along the pose's world direction within 2 degrees on both rigs

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Pelvis movement scales with leg length
    Given two rigged characters with different leg lengths
    When Jump and Down are baked onto both
    Then at each key frame the pelvis is displaced by the pose offset times that character's leg length

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Cycles are mirrored and loop
    Given a rigged character
    When Walk and Run are baked
    Then the second half of each cycle mirrors the first half
    And the last frame matches the first frame for Walk, Run, Idle, and FightIdle

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Provenance is recorded like a file clip
    Given a rigged character with built-in clips baked
    When the import result and the exported nmg-animations.json are read
    Then each built-in clip has its frame range, fps, and a source with library "builtin", skeleton "manny", file null, and the definition's sha256
    And the exported FBX holds the clip as an action

  @SCN008
  Scenario: Baking is repeatable
    Given a rigged character with a built-in clip already baked
    When the same clip is baked again
    Then the action is replaced with identical keyframes and provenance and no temporary data remains

  @SCN009
  Scenario: An unknown built-in clip is reported
    Given a rigged character
    When import_animations is called with library "builtin" and an unknown clip name
    Then the result is fallback required with anim.clip_not_found listing the built-in clip names and nothing is baked

  @SCN010
  Scenario: Invalid library selection is reported
    Given a rigged character
    When import_animations is called with both a folder and library "builtin", with neither, or with an unknown library value
    Then the result is fallback required with anim.library_invalid and the scene is unchanged

  @SCN011
  Scenario: File libraries behave as before
    Given a library folder with a valid library.json and clips
    When import_animations is called with the folder as today and built-in clips are baked onto the same rig
    Then the file clips' provenance is unchanged and both kinds appear in nmg-animations.json

  @SCN012
  Scenario: Existing preconditions still apply
    Given a collection with no SK_<Name> rig, or a call with a motion_prompt
    When import_animations is called with library "builtin"
    Then the result is anim.rig_missing or anim.text_motion_unsupported respectively

  @SCN013
  Scenario: The operator can select the built-in library
    Given the add-on operator nmggamedev.import_animations
    When it runs with the built-in library selected and no library folder
    Then the built-in clips are baked, the result is stored on scene.nmg_game_dev.last_result, and it returns FINISHED
